<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Comte de Grasse Squadron, 1988</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;This scenario assumes World War III starts in 1988.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;It is assumed that a rebellion in East Germany led to sporadic fighting between Soviet, Warsaw Pact, rebel, and NATO forces.&amp;nbsp; By early June, this had&amp;nbsp;escalated into open conflict.&amp;nbsp; Members of NATO formally agreed to take action against the Soviet Union on June 10, 1988.&amp;nbsp; Troops were already on the ground, but now fighting intensified.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;On June 12th, the Soviets used chemical weapons against NATO troops, and NATO responded the next day with tactical nuclear weapon strikes&amp;nbsp;against Warsaw Pact forces.&amp;nbsp; During the next several days, there were a number of additional nuclear exchanges in Europe and at sea.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;At present, the war has been "limited" in the sense&amp;nbsp;that no attacks have been made against the homeland territories of the four nuclear powers involved in the conflict, and as a result no counterforce strikes with&amp;nbsp;strategic nuclear weapons have taken place.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;During these first few critical&amp;nbsp;days of the war, one of the goals of the American&amp;nbsp;navy is to secure the vital sea lanes of the Atlantic so that convoys&amp;nbsp;will be able to&amp;nbsp;resupply NATO forces in the coming weeks.&amp;nbsp; As part of this effort, a task force centered around the American destroyer &lt;EM&gt;Comte de Grasse&lt;/EM&gt; has been assigned to patrol the waters near the Azores.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Please note that while your WRA is "weapons free," which means you will not automatically be hauled in front of a Board of Inquiry if you accidentally sink a fishing boat, this does not mean you should &lt;EM&gt;try&lt;/EM&gt; to sink them, or shoot airliners out of the sky, or&amp;nbsp;kill&amp;nbsp;harmless sea creatures&amp;nbsp;with depth charges, etc.&amp;nbsp; Quite apart from it being morally reprehensible behavior--we are&amp;nbsp;supposed to be the good guys, you know--it means you are wasting ammunition.&amp;nbsp; So knock it off.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;-------------------------------------------------------&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;A delta template .ini file has been included in the .zip file to assist in updating the scenario to any future versions of the database.&amp;nbsp; (The last time I updated the .ini file, Command said there were errors in it, but I have not been able to figure out what is wrong; it does not seem to do anything, but I have included the error message in the .zip file in case debugging is&amp;nbsp;needed in the future.)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Scenario Author: Mark Gellis&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
